\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces Absolute far-field predictions against published measurements, all four inflow spectra through the identical non-compact response \citep  {Amiet1975,RogerMoreau2010}: frozen von K\'arm\'an (black dashed), frozen Liepmann (grey dotted), the computed SC-ODT spectrum (grey, circles) and the computed clock-relaxed ODT spectrum (grey, triangles), each entered at the case's effective free-distortion strain. (\textit  {a,b}) NACA0012 of \citet  {PatersonAmiet1976} ($c=0.23$\,m, $u'_w/U\approx 4$--$5\%$, $\varLambda _f\approx 30$\,mm, observer $2.25$\,m overhead; Gershfeld thickness admittance applied identically to all four chains); (\textit  {c}) ECL flat plate of \citet  {Bampanis2022} ($c=0.10$\,m, $3$\,mm thick, $Tu=4.5\%$, $\varLambda =9$\,mm, $\varTheta =90^\circ $, $R=1.25$\,m); (\textit  {d}) ISVR flat plate of \citet  {Narayanan2015} ($c=0.15$\,m, $Tu=2.5\%$, $\varLambda =6$\,mm, $R=1.2$\,m). Black measured symbols lie in each case's stated comparison band (grey outside: background flags, facility contamination, thickness-breakdown frequency); spectra digitised from the published figures with per-figure calibration checks ($\pm 0.5$\,dB). The effective strain is a geometric estimate (potential-flow stagnation-line accumulation truncated at the eddy scale{\color {blue}\uwave {, varied over $\varLambda /4$--$\varLambda $}}); the {\color {red}\sout {shaded band spans truncation }}{\color {blue}\uwave {resulting spread in predicted level is }}at {\color {red}\sout {$\varLambda /4$--$\varLambda $}}{\color {blue}\uwave {most ${\approx }1$\,dB, comparable to the digitisation uncertainty, and is not shown}}.}}{41}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:expval}{{20}{41}{Absolute far-field predictions against published measurements, all four inflow spectra through the identical non-compact response \citep {Amiet1975,RogerMoreau2010}: frozen von K\'arm\'an (black dashed), frozen Liepmann (grey dotted), the computed SC-ODT spectrum (grey, circles) and the computed clock-relaxed ODT spectrum (grey, triangles), each entered at the case's effective free-distortion strain. (\textit {a,b}) NACA0012 of \citet {PatersonAmiet1976} ($c=0.23$\,m, $u'_w/U\approx 4$--$5\%$, $\Lambda _f\approx 30$\,mm, observer $2.25$\,m overhead; Gershfeld thickness admittance applied identically to all four chains); (\textit {c}) ECL flat plate of \citet {Bampanis2022} ($c=0.10$\,m, $3$\,mm thick, $Tu=4.5\%$, $\Lambda =9$\,mm, $\Theta =90^\circ $, $R=1.25$\,m); (\textit {d}) ISVR flat plate of \citet {Narayanan2015} ($c=0.15$\,m, $Tu=2.5\%$, $\Lambda =6$\,mm, $R=1.2$\,m). Black measured symbols lie in each case's stated comparison band (grey outside: background flags, facility contamination, thickness-breakdown frequency); spectra digitised from the published figures with per-figure calibration checks ($\pm 0.5$\,dB). The effective strain is a geometric estimate (potential-flow stagnation-line accumulation truncated at the eddy scale\DIFaddbeginFL \DIFaddFL {, varied over $\Lambda /4$--$\Lambda $}\DIFaddendFL ); the \DIFdelbeginFL \DIFdelFL {shaded band spans truncation }\DIFdelendFL \DIFaddbeginFL \DIFaddFL {resulting spread in predicted level is }\DIFaddendFL at \DIFdelbeginFL \DIFdelFL {$\Lambda /4$--$\Lambda $}\DIFdelendFL \DIFaddbeginFL \DIFaddFL {most ${\approx }1$\,dB, comparable to the digitisation uncertainty, and is not shown}\DIFaddendFL }{figure.caption.23}{}}
